  "passage": "At the end of each [[fiscal]] year, our accounting team prepares a financial [[statement]] that summarizes the company's income and spending. Last year, total [[revenue]] rose by twelve percent, mainly because we reduced unnecessary [[expenses]] and kept every department within its [[budget]].\n\nEvery [[transaction]] must be recorded carefully. Employees are required to keep each [[receipt]] so that the finance office can [[deduct]] business costs correctly and prepare for the annual [[audit]]. When a customer pays a large sum, we usually ask for a [[deposit]] first and allow the remainder to be paid in monthly [[installments]].\n\nThe auditor also checks whether any invoice is [[overdue]] and confirms that the account [[balance]] matches the bank records. Thanks to steady cash flow, the company was able to [[fund]] a new project without borrowing money. Management now considers the office building one of its most valuable [[assets]].",
