  "questions": [
    {"q": "Why did total revenue rise last year?", "choices": ["Because the company borrowed money.", "Because expenses were reduced and budgets were kept.", "Because the audit was postponed.", "Because customers paid in installments."], "answer": 1, "expl": "第1段落。総収益(revenue)が増えた主因は、不要な expenses(経費)を削減し、各部門が budget(予算)内に収まったことです。"},
    {"q": "Why must employees keep every receipt?", "choices": ["To pay in monthly installments.", "To increase the company's revenue.", "So that business costs can be deducted and the audit prepared.", "So that the building can be sold."], "answer": 2, "expl": "第2段落。領収書(receipt)を保管するのは、事業費を正しく deduct(控除)し、年次 audit(監査)に備えるためです。"},
    {"q": "In this passage, the word \"overdue\" is closest in meaning to", "choices": ["already paid", "past the due date", "recently issued", "carefully checked"], "answer": 1, "expl": "overdue は「(支払い・期限が)過ぎた」の意味で、past the due date に相当します。invoice(請求書)とともに頻出します。"}
  ]
